.TH VIRCON2WAV 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
vircon2wav \- convert a Vircon32 sound back into a WAV file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vircon2wav
.RB [ \-o
.IR output.wav ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I input.vsnd
.br
.B vircon2wav
.B \-\-help
.br
.B vircon2wav
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vircon2wav
reads a VSND sound (as made by
.BR wav2vircon (1)
or extracted from a cartridge by
.BR unpackrom (1))
and writes it as an uncompressed PCM WAV file: 16-bit stereo at
44100 Hz, which is how the console plays every sound. The sound must
hold between 1 and 268435456 samples, and its file size must match
the length in its header.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output.wav"
Write the WAV file to
.IR output.wav .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output path is the input path with its extension replaced by
.IR .wav .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report the sound length and each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The WAV file was written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "vircon2wav: error: description" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wav2vircon (1),
.BR unpackrom (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 WAV extractor was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
